          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %strong Gray tensor product
            is a “better” replacement for the cartesian product of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+2-categories"} strict 2-categories
            with respect to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudonatural+transformations"} pseudonatural transformations
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{2}
            which has two objects, 0 and 1, one non-identity morphism
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0\to 1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ×
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{2}\times\mathbf{2}
            is a commuting square, while the Gray tensor product
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{2}\otimes\mathbf{2}
            is a square which commutes up to isomorphism.
          %p
            More generally, given
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-categories"} 2-categories
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-functor"} 2-functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo ×
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mn 2
                  %mo →
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C\times\mathbf{2} \to D
            consists of two 2-functors
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C\to D
            and a strict 2-natural transformation between them, while a 2-functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mn 2
                  %mo →
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C\otimes\mathbf{2} \to D
            consists of two 2-functors
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C\to D
            and a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudonatural+transformation"} pseudonatural transformation
            between them.
          %h2#Preliminaries Preliminaries
          %p Throughout, write
          #eq:2Cat.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 2
                  %mi Cat
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi CAT
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  2Cat \in CAT
          %p
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/very+large+category"} very large
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            whose
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
                are
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+2-categories"} strict 2-categories
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
                are
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+2-functors"} strict 2-functors
          %p
            For
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mn 2
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X, Y \in 2Cat
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi Cat
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Hom_{2Cat}(X,Y) \in Set
          %p
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom+set"} hom set
            of this 2-category, hence for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+2-functors"} strict 2-functors
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to Y
          %p
            Of course, there is not just a set but a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+2-category"} strict 2-category
            of such functors. Specifically, we write
          #eq:Ps.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (2)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ps
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mn 2
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Ps(Y,Z)
                  \\in
                  2Cat
          %p
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+2-category"} strict
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-functor+2-category"} 2-functor 2-category
            whose
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
                are
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+2-functors"} strict 2-functors
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Y
                        %mo →
                        %mi Z
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \to Z
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-morphisms"} 1-morphisms
                are
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudonatural+transformations"} pseudonatural transformations
                between these,
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-morphisms"} 2-morphisms
                are
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modifications"} modifications
                between those,
          %p
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
            operations the canonical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horizontal+composition"} horizontal composition
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertical+composition"} vertical composition
            of this data.
          %p
            (cf.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#JohnsonYau20"} Johnson &amp; Yau 2020, Ntn. 12.2.24
          %p
            The point of the Gray tensor product may be regarded as bringing out the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enrichment
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 2
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2Cat
            by these hom 2-categories
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ps
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ps(-,-)
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:Ps"} (2)
          %h2#Definition Definition
          %p
          .num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              The
              %em Gray tensor product
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            #eq:GrayTensorAsFunctor.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (3)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi Gray
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mn 2
                    %mi Cat
                    %mo ×
                    %mn 2
                    %mi Cat
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mn 2
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\otimes_{Gray}
                    \\;\colon\;
                    2Cat \times 2Cat \longrightarrow 2Cat
            %p given by (…).
            %p
          %p
            (cf.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#JohnsonYau20"} Johnson &amp; Yau 2020, Def. 12.2.5
          %h2#Properties Properties
          %h3#homadjunction_and_closure Hom-adjunction and closure
          %p First of all:
          %p
          .num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              The Gray tensor product
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:GrayTensorAsFunctor"} (3)
              makes
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2Cat
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:2Cat"} (1)
              into a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+unit"} tensor unit
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+category"} terminal
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ast
              (hence a
              = succeed "):" do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semicartesian+monoidal+category"} semicartesian monoidal category
            #eq:2CatAsAMonoidalCategory.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (4)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mi Cat
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi Gray
                    %mo ,
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi MonCAT
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\big(
                    2Cat, \otimes_{Gray}, \ast
                    \\big)
                    \\in MonCAT
                    \\,.
            %p
          %p
            (cf.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#JohnsonYau20"} Johnson &amp; Yau 2020, Thm. 12.2.23
          %p As such, the characteristic property of the Gray tensor product is that:
          %p
          #HomIsomorphism.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              There are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+bijections"} natural bijections
            #eq:TheHomIsomorphism.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (5)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mi Cat
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi Gray
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mi Cat
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Ps
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Hom_{2Cat}(X \otimes_{Gray} Y, Z)
                    \\simeq
                    Hom_{2Cat}\big(X, Ps(Y,Z)\big)
                    \\,,
            %p
              natural in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Y
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Z
                      %mo ∈
                      %mn 2
                      %mi Cat
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X, Y, Z \in 2 Cat
            %p
          %p
            (cf.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#JohnsonYau20"} Johnson &amp; Yau 2020, Prop. 12.2.27 with Thm. 12.2.20
          %p
            Since
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:TheHomIsomorphism"} (5)
            are the
            %a{:href => "adjoint+functor#InTermsOfHomIsomorphism"} hom isomorphism
            for an
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom"} internal hom
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor"} adjunction
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi Gray
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi Ps
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\big(
                  (-) \otimes_{Gray} Y
                  \\big)
                  \\;\dashv\;
                  Ps(Y,-)
                  \\,,
          %p
            Prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HomIsomorphism"}
            says that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mi Cat
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi Gray
                  %mo ,
                  %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (2Cat, \otimes_{Gray}, \ast)
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:2CatAsAMonoidalCategory"} (4)
            is in a fact
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+category"} closed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+closed+monoidal+category"} symmetric closed monoidal category
            (with tensor product being the Gray tensor and) with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom"} internal hom
            given by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ps
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ps(-,-)
            = succeed "." do
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:Ps"} (2)
          %h3#further_properties Further properties
          %p
          #BiequivalenceToCartesianProduct.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              For
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Y
                      %mo ∈
                      %mn 2
                      %mi Cat
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X, Y \in 2Cat
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} Cartesian product
              (discarding the interchangers) is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+2-categories"} equivalence of 2-categories
              (in fact an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/acyclic+fibration"} acyclic fibration
              in the
              = succeed "):" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+model+structure+on+2-categories"} canonical model structure on 2-groupoids
            #eq:ComparisonMapGrayToCartesian.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (6)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi Gray
                    %mi Y
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mphantom
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mo −
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi W
                        %mo ∩
                        %mi Fib
                        %mphantom
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mo −
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Y
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X \otimes_Gray Y
                    \\xrightarrow{\phantom{--}
                    \\in W \cap Fib
                    \\phantom{--}}
                    X \times Y
                    \\,.
            %p
          (cf.
          = succeed ")" do
            %a{:href => "#Lack2002"} Lack 2002, top of p. 7
          %p
          #GrayDiagonalsForCofibant2Groupoids.num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              While the Gray monoidal structure
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:2CatAsAMonoidalCategory"} (4)
              is (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semicartesian+monoidal+category"} semicartesian
              but) not a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category+with+diagonals"} monoidal category with diagonals
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:ComparisonMapGrayToCartesian"} (6)
              implies immediately that good “Gray-diagonals” do exist for 2-groupoids which are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrant+object"} cofibrant
              in the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+model+structure+on+strict+2-groupoids"} canonical model structure
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lifting"} lifting
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mn 2
                    %msup
                      %mi Grpd
                      %mi cof
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⊢
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "center center center", :displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                          %msub
                            %mo ⊗
                            %mi Gray
                          %mi X
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                            %mrow
                              %msup
                                %mo
                                %mo ∃
                          %mo ↗
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                        %mtd
                          %munder
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mi diag
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                          %mo ×
                          %mi X
                          %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                            %mrow
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X \in 2Grpd^{cof}
                    \\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;
                    \\vdash
                    \\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;
                    \\begin{array}{ccc}
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    X \otimes_{Gray} X
                    \\\
                    \&amp;
                    {\mathllap{^{\exists}}}\nearrow
                    \&amp;
                    \\big\downarrow
                    \\\
                    X
                    \&amp;\underset{diag}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    X \times X
                    \\mathrlap{\,,}
                    \\end{array}
            %p
              of, at the bottom, the ordinary
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagonal+map"} diagonal map
              into the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} Cartesian product
          %p
          #UnderSimplicialNerve.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              Under passage to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+nerve+of+a+bicategory"} nerves
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+2-groupoids"} strict 2-groupoids
            #eq:SimplicialNerveOf2Groupoids.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (7)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mn 2
                    %mi Grpd
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi sSet
                    %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    N
                    \\;\colon\;
                    2Grpd \longrightarrow sSet
                    \\mathrlap{\,,}
            %ol
              %li
                %p the nerve of a Gray tensor product of 2-groupoids,
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} Cartesian product
                  (cf.
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %em
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+of+simplices"} product of simplices
            %p
              are related by a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+weak+equivalence"} simplicial weak equivalence
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/acyclic+Kan+fibration"} acyclic Kan fibration
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi Y
                        %mo ∈
                        %mn 2
                        %mi Grpd
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo ⊢
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi Gray
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi Fib
                        %mo ∩
                        %mi W
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ×
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathllap{
                    X, Y \in 2Grpd
                    \\;\;\;\;\;\;\;
                    \\vdash
                    \\;\;\;\;\;\;\;
                    }
                    N\big(
                    X \otimes_{Gray} Y
                    \\big)
                    \\xrightarrow{ \in Fib \cap W }
                    N(X) \times N(Y)
                    \\mathrlap{\,.}
            %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+nerve+of+2-categories"} nerve
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:SimplicialNerveOf2Groupoids"} (7)
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+Quillen+functor"} right Quillen functor
              from the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+model+structure+on+2-categories"} canonical model structure on 2-groupoids
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} classical model structure on simplicial sets
              (
              %a{:href => "#Lack2002"}> Lack 2002, end of p. 29
              , following
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "canonical+model+structure+on+2-categories#MoerdijkSvensson93"} Moerdijk &amp; Svensson 1993
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/acyclic+fibrations"} acyclic fibrations
              and hence sends the comparison map
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:ComparisonMapGrayToCartesian"} (6)
              to an acyclic Kan fibration.
          %p
          #InternalHomUnderSimplicialNerve.num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              %br/
              Related to Prop.
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#UnderSimplicialNerve"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mi Ps
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi N
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    N\big(
                    Ps(X,Y)
                    \\big)
                    \\longrightarrow
                    N(Y)^{N(X)}
            %p
              (from the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+nerve+of+a+bicategory"} simplicial nerve
              of
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:Ps"} (2)
              to the
              %a{:href => "function+complex#InSimplicialSets"} simplicial function complex
              between the separate nerves of the arguments) and this is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+weak+equivalence"} simplicial weak equivalence
              when
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrant+object"} cofibrant
              in the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+model+structure+on+2Grpd"} canonical model structure on 2-groupoids
              %br/
          %p
            This is due to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Campbell"} Alexander Campbell
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "https://nforum.ncatlab.org/discussion/11750/gray-tensor-product/#Item_21"} here
          %h2#further_remarks Further remarks
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                When considered with this monoidal structure,
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi Cat
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2Cat
                is often called
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Gray
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Gray
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gray-category"} Gray-categories
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched
                over
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Gray
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Gray
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semi-strict+infinity-category"} semi-strict
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/3-categories"} 3-categories
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi Cat
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2Cat
                with its cartesian product are
                %em strict
                3-categories, which are not as useful. This is one precise sense in which the Gray tensor product is “more correct” than the cartesian product.
            %li
              %p There are also versions of the Gray tensor product in which pseudonatural transformations are replaced by lax or oplax ones. (In fact, these were the ones originally defined by Gray.)
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Gray
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Gray
                is actually a monoidal
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
                (that is, a model category with a monoidal structure that interacts well with the model structure), which
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi Cat
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2Cat
                with the cartesian product is not. In particular, the cartesian product of two cofibrant 2-categories need not be cofibrant. This is another precise sense in which the Gray tensor product is “more correct” than the cartesian product.
            %li
              %p
                The cartesian monoidal structure is sometimes called the “black” product, since the square
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mo ×
                      %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2\times 2
                is “completely filled in” (i.e. it commutes). There is another “white” tensor product in which the square
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mo □
                      %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2\Box 2
                is “not filled in at all” (doesn’t commute at all), and the “gray” tensor product is in between the two (the square commutes up to an isomorphism). This is a pun on the name of John Gray, for whom the Gray tensor product is named. The “white” tensor product is also called the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/funny+tensor+product"} funny tensor product
            %li
              %p
                There are generalizations to
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory"} higher categories
                of the Gray tensor product. In particular there is a tensor product on
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+omega-category"} strict omega-categories
                – the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Crans-Gray+tensor+product"} Crans-Gray tensor product
                – which is such that restricted to strict 2-categories it reproduces the Gray tensor product.
            %li
              %p
                A
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+category"} closed monoidal structure
                on
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+omega-category"} strict omega-categories
                is introduced by Al-Agl, Brown and Steiner. This uses an equivalence between the categories of strict (globular) omega categories and of strict cubical omega categories with connections; the construction of the closed monoidal structure on the latter category is direct and generalises that for strict cubical omega groupoids with connections established by Brown and Higgins.
            %li
              %p
                The Gray tensor product cannot be extended to a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-functor"} 2-functor
                (or 3-functor) on the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
                of 2-categories, 2-functors,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-natural+transformations"} 2-natural transformations
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modifications"} modifications
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "https://mathoverflow.net/a/459360"} this MathOverflow answer
          %h2#related_entries Related entries
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Crans-Gray+tensor+product"} Crans-Gray tensor product
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+Gray+tensor+product"} generalized Gray tensor product
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Verity-Gray+tensor+product"} Verity-Gray tensor product
          %h2#references References
          %h3#in_2category_theory In 2-category theory
          %p
            Original discussion of the Gray tensor product in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category+theory"} 2-category theory
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+W.+Gray"}> John W. Gray
                , Theorem 1, 4.14 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Adjointness+for+2-Categories"} Formal category theory: Adjointness for 2-categories
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 391
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BFb0061280"} doi:10.1007/BFb0061280
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+W.+Gray"}> John W. Gray
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Coherence for the Tensor Product of 2-Categories, and Braid Groups
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Algebra, Topology, and Category Theory
          %p
            In the context of the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+model+structure+on+2-categories"} canonical model structure on 2-categories
          %ul
            %li#Lack2002
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stephen+Lack"}> Stephen Lack
              \:
              = succeed "," do
                %em A Quillen model structure for 2-categories
              %strong 26
              2 (2002) 171-205 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1023/A:1020305604826"}> doi:10.1023/A:1020305604826
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Lack-ModelOn2Cat.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://zbmath.org/?q=an%3A1017.18005"} zbmath
          %p Further discussion:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ronnie+Brown"}> Ronnie Brown
                ,
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Philip+Higgins"} Philip Higgins
                = succeed ",J." do
                  %em
                    Tensor products and homotopies for
                    = succeed "-groupoids" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi ω
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
                %strong 47
                (1987) 1-33
                %em
                  lbrack;doi:
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-4049(87%2990099-5"}> 10.1016/0022-4049(87)90099-5
                  , (
                  %a{:href => "https://pdfs.semanticscholar.org/3323/d82ed1effb1953a6af573aab2e3fb0b02394.pdf"}> pdf
                  \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+Gordon"}> Robert Gordon
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Power"} John Power
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ross+Street"} Ross Street
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Coherence for tricategories
                %strong 117
                558 (1995) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1090/memo/0558"}> doi:10.1090/memo/0558
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://bookstore.ams.org/memo-117-558/"} ams:memo-117-558
            %li
              %p
                F.A. Al-Agl, R. Brown and R. Steiner,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Multiple categories: the equivalence between a globular and cubical approach
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1006/aima.2001.2069"} 10.1006/aima.2001.2069
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0007009"} math/0007009
          %p Comprehensive review:
          %ul
            %li#JohnsonYau20
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Niles+Johnson"}> Niles Johnson
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Donald+Yau"} Donald Yau
              = succeed "," do
                %em 2-Dimensional Categories
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/2002.06055"} arXiv:2002.06055
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://oxford.universitypressscholarship.com/view/10.1093/oso/9780198871378.001.0001/oso-9780198871378"} doi:10.1093/oso/9780198871378.001.0001
          %p
            On the Gray tensor product as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+Kan+extension"} left Kan extension
            of a tensor product on the full subcategory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cu
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cu
            of
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2Cat
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ross+Street"}> Ross Street
              , p. 16 of:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Gray’s tensor product of 2-categories
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://maths.mq.edu.au/~street/GrayTensor.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            A general theory of lax tensor products, unifying Gray tensor products with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Crans-Gray+tensor+product"} Crans-Gray tensor product
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Batanin"}> Michael Batanin
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Denis-Charles+Cisinski"} Denis-Charles Cisinski
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mark+Weber"} Mark Weber
              %em Multitensor lifting and strictly unital higher category theory
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1209.2776"}> arXiv:1209.2776
              )
          %p A proof that the Gray tensor product does form a monoidal structure, based only on its universal property, is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Bourke"}> John Bourke
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nick+Gurski"} Nick Gurski
              = succeed "," do
                %em The Gray tensor product via factorisation
              %strong 25
              (2017) p603-624, doi:
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s10485-016-9467-6"}> 10.1007/s10485-016-9467-6
              , arXiv:
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1508.07789"} 1508.07789
          %p
            On its generalization to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gray-category"} Gray-categories
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sjoerd+Crans"}> Sjoerd Crans
              \. “A tensor product for
              = succeed "-categories\u201D." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Gray
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Gray
              = succeed "," do
                %em Theory and applications of categories
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/1999/n2/5-02abs.html"} tac
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/1999/n2/n2.pdf"} pdf
          %h3#in_enhanced_2category_theory In enhanced 2-category theory
          %p
